    <h2>2. Marketplace Role &amp; Mandatory Consumer Disclosures (Gov. Decree 45/2014, Section 11)</h2>
    <p>
      In accordance with Section 11 of Hungarian Government Decree 45/2014 (II. 26.) and the EU Omnibus Directive on online marketplaces, buyers are informed prior to submitting a hold request that:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Seller Status (Private Individual vs. Verified Store):</strong> Unless a seller is explicitly marked with a <strong>"Verified Store"</strong> badge, the seller is acting as a <strong>private individual (<em>magánszemély</em>)</strong> and not as a business/trader.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No Statutory 14-Day Withdrawal Right Against Private Sellers:</strong> When purchasing from a private individual, the sales contract is concluded between two private individuals (C2C) under the Hungarian Civil Code (Act V of 2013 — Ptk.). Consequently, <strong>EU and Hungarian consumer protection rights applicable only against businesses — including the statutory 14-day right of withdrawal without reason — do NOT apply</strong> to the transaction.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Contractual Responsibility:</strong> The sales contract is formed exclusively between the seller and the buyer. TCG XChange is not a party to the sale, charges no commission, does not process or hold payments, and bears no liability for payment, shipping, or card condition between users.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Your Account</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You must be at least <strong>16 years old</strong> to create an account.</li>
      <li>One person, one account. Creating extra accounts to review yourself, inflate sales numbers, or bypass a suspension is prohibited.</li>
      <li>Use a display name that does not impersonate another person or store, and keep your password secure.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How Marketplace Trades Work</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>A buyer adds cards to their cart, selects a handover method, and submits a hold request.</li>
      <li>The seller accepts or rejects the request. Accepting reserves the cards for that buyer.</li>
      <li>Both parties agree on payment (e.g., cash in person or direct bank transfer) and handover details in <strong>Messages</strong>. TCG XChange does not process payments or hold funds.</li>
      <li>Once the cards have been handed over or shipped, the seller marks the order as <em>Handed over</em>.</li>
      <li>The buyer confirms receipt once the cards arrive, completing the trade. If the buyer does not respond within 14 days of handover and raises no issue, the seller may mark the trade completed.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      See the <a href="/help/shipping">Shipping &amp; handover guide</a> and <a href="/help/selling">Seller guidelines</a> for practical details.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Rules for Sellers &amp; Tax Notice</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Only list authentic cards that you own and physically have ready to hand over. Describe the set, version, finish, and condition accurately, with real photos where applicable.</li>
      <li>The listing price and shipping fees you configure are the total price the buyer agrees to; do not add hidden charges afterwards.</li>
      <li><strong>Hungarian Tax Notice:</strong> Under Hungarian personal income tax law (SZJA), occasional sales of personal movable property by private individuals are tax-exempt up to 600,000 HUF gross revenue (or 200,000 HUF profit) per calendar year. Sellers trading regularly for business profit (<em>üzletszerűen</em>) are solely responsible for registering as a business/sole proprietor and issuing tax-compliant invoices.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Rules for Buyers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Only request holds you genuinely intend to complete, and pay as agreed with the seller.</li>
      <li>Confirm receipt only after you have received and inspected the cards.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Ranking &amp; Review Transparency</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Search &amp; Sort Ranking:</strong> Catalog and marketplace results are ordered strictly by the user-selected sort mode (e.g., Lowest Price, Card Number, Rarity, Quantity, Name). There are no paid placements or hidden ranking boosts.</li>
      <li><strong>Review Authenticity:</strong> Reviews can only be submitted by the actual buyer and seller of a trade that was marked completed on TCG XChange, limited to one review per party per completed order.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Prohibited Conduct &amp; Notice-and-Action (EU DSA Art. 16)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Counterfeit or proxy cards sold as authentic, or listing items you do not possess;</li>
      <li>Scams, payment fraud, harassment, threats, hate speech, or spam;</li>
      <li>Fake or coerced reviews, scraping, or attempting to compromise accounts or infrastructure.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Reporting Illegal Content (Notice &amp; Action):</strong> Anyone may report counterfeit listings, scams, copyright infringement, or illegal content by emailing <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with a link/description of the content and the reason for the report. We review reports promptly and may remove listings or suspend accounts that violate these terms or applicable law, notifying affected users with the reasons for the decision.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Disclaimers, Dispute Resolution &amp; Governing Law</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>TCG XChange is provided "as is" and free of charge. Market reference prices (from Cardmarket / TCGplayer) are estimates for informational purposes only.</li>
      <li>These terms are governed by <strong>Hungarian law</strong> (in particular Act V of 2013 on the Civil Code and Act CVIII of 2001 on Electronic Commerce).</li>
      <li>For complaints or questions, contact <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Consumers in Hungary may also contact the competent Conciliation Board (<a href="https://bekeltetes.hu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">bekeltetes.hu</a>) or consumer protection authority.</li>
    </ul>
